1
00:00:06,039 --> 00:00:10,840
Where's Papa going with that axe? said Fern to her mother as they were setting

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:17,000
the table for breakfast. Out to the hog house, replied Mrs. Arable. Some pigs

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,079
were born last night. I don't see why he needs an axe, continued Fern, who was

4
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:29,879
only eight. Well, said her mother. One of the pigs is a runt. It's very small

5
00:00:29,879 --> 00:00:37,719
and weak, and it'll never amount to anything. So, your father has decided to do away with it.

6
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:44,920
Do away with it? Shrieked Fern. You mean kill it? Just because it's smaller than

7
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:50,200
the others? Mrs. Darable put a picture of cream on the table. "Don't yell,

8
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,959
Fern," she said. "Your father is right.

9
00:00:53,959 --> 00:00:59,560
The pig would probably die anyway." Fern pushed a chair out of the way and ran

10
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:05,400
outdoors. The grass was wet and the earth smelled of springtime.

11
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:10,280
Fern's sneakers were sping by the time she caught up with her father.

12
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,920
"Please don't kill it," she sobbed.

13
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:19,799
"It's unfair." Mr. Parable stopped walking. "Fern," he said gently. "You

14
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:22,200
will have to learn to control yourself."

15
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:29,318
"Control myself?" yelled Fern. "This is a matter of life and death, and you talk

16
00:01:29,318 --> 00:01:31,959
about controlling myself."

17
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:37,800
Tears ran down her cheeks, and she took hold of the axe and tried to pull it out

18
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,520
of her father's hand.

19
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:46,199
"Fern," said Mr. Arable. I know more about raising a litter of pigs than you

20
00:01:46,199 --> 00:01:53,800
do. A weakling makes trouble. Now run along. But it's unfair, cried Fern. The

21
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:59,000
pig couldn't help being born small, could it? If I had been very small at

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,199
birth, would you have killed me?

23
00:02:02,199 --> 00:02:04,840
Mr. Arable smiled.

24
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:11,080
Certainly not, he said, looking down at his daughter with love. But this is

25
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:17,479
different. A little girl is one thing. A little runty pig is another. I see no

26
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:23,800
difference, replied Fern, still hanging on to the axe. This is the most terrible

27
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:31,158
case of injustice I ever heard of. A queer look came over John Arabel's face.

28
00:02:31,158 --> 00:02:34,280
He seemed almost ready to cry himself.

29
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:39,560
"All right," he said. "You go back to the house, and I'll bring the runt when

30
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:45,158
I come in. I'll let you start it on a bottle like a baby. Then you'll see what

31
00:02:45,158 --> 00:02:47,800
trouble a pig can be.

32
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:52,598
When Mr. Arable returned to the house half an hour later, he carried a carton

33
00:02:52,598 --> 00:02:58,840
under his arm. Fern was upstairs changing her sneakers. The kitchen table

34
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:04,840
was set for breakfast, and the room smelled of coffee, bacon, damp plaster,

35
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:11,560
and wood smoke from the stove. Put it on her chair, said Mrs. Arable. Mr. Arable

36
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,199
set the carton down at Fern's place.

37
00:03:14,199 --> 00:03:20,519
Then he walked to the sink and washed his hands and dried them on the roller towel.

38
00:03:20,519 --> 00:03:27,080
Fern came slowly down the stairs. Her eyes were red from crying.

39
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:33,560
As she approached her chair, the carton wobbled and there was a scratching noise.

40
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:39,000
Fern looked at her father. Then she lifted the lid of the carton. There

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:46,439
inside, looking up at her, was the newborn pig. It was a white one. The

42
00:03:46,439 --> 00:03:53,000
morning light shone through its ears, turning them pink. "He's yours," said

43
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:59,879
Mr. Arable, saved from an untimely death. "And may the good Lord forgive me

44
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:02,918
for this foolishness."

45
00:04:02,918 --> 00:04:10,839
Fern couldn't take her eyes off the tiny pig. Oh," she whispered. "Oh, look at

46
00:04:10,839 --> 00:04:18,519
him. He's absolutely perfect." She closed the carton carefully. First, she

47
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:23,800
kissed her father. Then, she kissed her mother. Then, she opened the lid again,

48
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:29,240
lifted the pig out, and held it against her cheek. At this moment, her brother

49
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,918
Avery came into the room.

50
00:04:32,918 --> 00:04:39,720
Avery was 10. He was heavily armed, an air rifle in one hand, a wooden dagger

51
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,918
in the other. What's that? He demanded.

52
00:04:42,918 --> 00:04:48,918
What's Fern got? She's got a guest for breakfast, said Mrs. Arable. Wash your

53
00:04:48,918 --> 00:04:51,560
hands and face, Avery.

54
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:57,399
Let's see it, said Avery, setting his gun down. You called that miserable

55
00:04:57,399 --> 00:05:04,759
thing a pig. That's a fine specimen of a pig. It's no bigger than a white rat.

56
00:05:04,759 --> 00:05:09,000
Wash up and eat your breakfast, Avery, said his mother. The school bus will be

57
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:15,079
along in half an hour. Can I have a pig, too, Pop? asked Avery.

58
00:05:15,079 --> 00:05:22,759
No, I only distribute pigs to early risers, said Mr. Arable. Fern was up a

59
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:26,360
daylight trying to rid the world of injustice.

60
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:33,720
As a result, she now has a pig. A small one to be sure, but nevertheless a pig.

61
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:40,279
It just shows what can happen if a person gets out of bed promptly. Let's eat.

62
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:46,519
But Fern couldn't eat until her pig had had a drink of milk. Mrs. Arable found a

63
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:51,560
baby's nursing bottle and a rubber nipple. She poured warm milk into the

64
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:56,680
bottle, fitted the nipple over the top, and handed it to Fern. Give him his

65
00:05:56,680 --> 00:06:02,199
breakfast, she said. A minute later, Fern was seated on the floor in the

66
00:06:02,199 --> 00:06:07,079
corner of the kitchen with her infant between her knees, teaching it to suck

67
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:15,639
from the bottle. The pig, although tiny, had a good appetite and caught on quickly.

68
00:06:15,639 --> 00:06:18,360
The school bus honked from the road.

69
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:24,439
"Run," commanded Mrs. Arable, taking the pig from Fern and slipping a donut into

70
00:06:24,439 --> 00:06:30,839
her hand. Avery grabbed his gun and another donut. The children ran out to

71
00:06:30,839 --> 00:06:37,160
the road and climbed into the bus. Fern took no notice of the others in the bus.

72
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:42,759
She just sat and stared out of the window, thinking what a blissful world

73
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:49,560
it was, and how lucky she was to have entire charge of a pig.

74
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:55,720
By the time the bus reached school, Fern had named her pet, selecting the most

75
00:06:55,720 --> 00:07:01,639
beautiful name she could think of. "Its name is Wilbur," she whispered to

76
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:07,478
herself. She was still thinking about the pig when the teacher said, "Fern,

77
00:07:07,478 --> 00:07:10,199
what is the capital of Pennsylvania?"

78
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:18,000
"Wilbur," replied Fern dreily. The pupils giggled.

79
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:21,680
Fern blushed.

80
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:27,399
Chapter 2.

81
00:07:27,399 --> 00:07:28,899
Wilbur.

82
00:07:28,899 --> 00:07:30,000
[Music]
